id: SCA-037
title: Python .pth file with import (auto-execution on startup)
category: supply-chain
severity: error
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .pth
  exclude_paths: test/ node_modules/ .git/ vendor/
patterns:
  - regex: ^import\s
    message: Python executes code in .pth files starting with import on every interpreter startup — silently, with no opt-in. The Hades/Shai-Hulud PyPI campaigns used this vector.
fix: Audit all .pth files in your environment. They should only contain directory paths, never import statements. Remove any .pth file with executable code.
